<!-- The W.D. Wis. motion brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs; docs/EVAL-LOOP.md,
     "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; no W.D. Wis. rule names a face,
     rules.md WIWD-LEN-001) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (480 twips: typst
     pitch-body, double spacing at 12 pt as the exemplar) with a half-inch first-line indent; single lines in 13.8 pt
     boxes (276 twips: typst pitch-single); headings on the body pitch with no space of their own. Letter page with
     one-inch margins (the exemplar's), the page number centred at 11 pt in a single-pitch line whose box ends 0.5 in
     above the page edge (typst footer-distance). docx/wiwd-motion-brief.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing.
     Twips: 20 x pt. -->
